The system's printf family reads %lld and %llo as %ld and %lo: it takes
one 32-bit word of the 64-bit argument (on the 68k the high one, zero
for any size under 4 GB) and misreads every argument after it, and its
sscanf stores 32 bits into a long long.  tar wrote the size field of
every header with sprintf("%11.11llo"), so an archive made here would
have recorded every file as empty.  Each such conversion now goes
through snprintf or vsnprintf (libamixc99, which formats long long), and
the device numbers are read with strtoll.

